import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentFormalModule
import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.ClosedImmersion

/-!
# Pushforward of ideal powers along a closed immersion

Source: Stacks Project, Cohomology of Schemes, proof of Lemma 088A, lines 6961--6968;
Morphisms, Lemmas 01QO and 01QY 
(blueprint: lem-weil-pbc-closed-immersion-pushforward-ideal-powers).
-/

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme

noncomputable section

/-- Pushforward along a closed immersion identifies powers of an extended ideal with
powers of the original ideal, and identifies the resulting quotient modules.
Source: Stacks Project, proof of Lemma 088A, lines 6961--6968 
(blueprint: lem-weil-pbc-closed-immersion-pushforward-ideal-powers).
Proof:
1. By lem-weil-pbc-closed-immersion-affine-cover-criterion, over an affine V = Spec R
of X the inverse image is Spec(R/J(V)) and the structure ring map is surjective, with
kernel J(V) (def-sbc-closed-immersion-ideal-sheaf). Pushforward evaluates on inverse
images with restriction of scalars (def-pc-module-pullback).
2. Apply lem-weil-pbc-module-pullback-ideal-quotient to I and i. The extended ideal is
quasi-coherent and has affine sections generated by the image of I(V). Surjectivity
makes this image itself an ideal, proving clause (1).
3. By lem-weil-pbc-ideal-times-quasi-coherent-affine-sections, powers, products and
quotients are quasi-coherent. By lem-weil-pbc-closed-immersion-pushforward-annihilated,
their direct images are also quasi-coherent.
4. The affine-section lemma gives upstairs products (I(V)(R/J(V)))^n M, downstairs
products I(V)^n M, and quotient projections surjective with these kernels.
5. For the surjection pi : R -> R/J(V), pi(I)^n = pi(I^n). The action on M through
pi therefore identifies (I(R/J(V)))^n M with I^n M.
6. The two submodules agree on the affine basis by step 5. Restrict sections to this
basis and glue inside either subsheaf to prove equality on all opens.
7. The pushforward quotient projection kills the common submodule, so factors uniquely
through the downstairs cokernel (def-weil-pbc-coherent-formal-module).
8. On affines the projections are surjective with the same kernel, so the factor is
bijective. Injectivity and local preimages glue on the affine basis, giving an isomorphism.
9. Linear maps preserve ideal products. The naturality composites agree after the
quotient projection, so agree by its epimorphism property. For m >= n, inclusion of
I^m G in I^n G yields reduction maps. Both level-compatibility composites agree after
the level-m projection, and hence agree by the same cokernel property.
-/
theorem closedImmersion_pushforward_idealPowers
    {X Z : Scheme.{u}} (i : Z ⟶ X) [IsClosedImmersion i]
    (I : X.IdealSheafData) :
    (I.comap i).toModules.IsQuasicoherent ∧
    (∀ U : X.affineOpens,
      ∃ (V : Z.affineOpens) (hV : V.1 = i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1),
        (I.comap i).ideal V =
          (I.ideal U).map (i.appLE U.1 V.1 (by simp [hV])).hom) ∧
    (∀ (G : Z.Modules) [G.IsQuasicoherent] (n : ℕ), 1 ≤ n →
      Subobject.mk (image.ι ((Modules.pushforward i).map (idealModuleProductι
        (idealSheafPower (I.comap i).toModulesι n).2 G))) =
        Subobject.mk (image.ι (idealModuleProductι
          (idealSheafPower I.toModulesι n).2 ((Modules.pushforward i).obj G)))) ∧
    ∃ ρ : (∀ (G : Z.Modules) [G.IsQuasicoherent] (n : ℕ), 1 ≤ n →
        (formalModuleQuotient I n ((Modules.pushforward i).obj G) ≅
        (Modules.pushforward i).obj (formalModuleQuotient (I.comap i) n G))),
      (∀ (G : Z.Modules) [G.IsQuasicoherent] (n : ℕ) (hn : 1 ≤ n),
        formalModuleQuotientπ I n ((Modules.pushforward i).obj G) ≫ (ρ G n hn).hom =
          (Modules.pushforward i).map (formalModuleQuotientπ (I.comap i) n G)) ∧
      (∀ (G H : Z.Modules) [G.IsQuasicoherent] [H.IsQuasicoherent] (u : G ⟶ H)
          (n : ℕ) (hn : 1 ≤ n),
        formalModuleQuotientMap I ((Modules.pushforward i).map u)
            (Nat.le_refl n) ≫ (ρ H n hn).hom =
          (ρ G n hn).hom ≫ (Modules.pushforward i).map
            (formalModuleQuotientMap (I.comap i) u (Nat.le_refl n))) ∧
      (∀ (G : Z.Modules) [G.IsQuasicoherent] (m n : ℕ) (h : n ≤ m) (hn : 1 ≤ n),
        formalModuleQuotientMap I (𝟙 ((Modules.pushforward i).obj G)) h ≫
            (ρ G n hn).hom =
          (ρ G m (le_trans hn h)).hom ≫ (Modules.pushforward i).map
            (formalModuleQuotientMap (I.comap i) (𝟙 G) h)) := by
  sorry

end
end AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme
